% jfb 1
$$\int \frac{\text{d} x}{a x} = \frac{1}{a} \ln |x| + C$$
---

# Solution

$[\mathbb{R}::\text{div}]$
$a x < 0 \to \square\ \alpha _1$
$a x = 0 \to \blacksquare$
$a x > 0 \to \square\ \alpha _2$
---

## $\alpha _1: a x < 0$

$$\ln |x| = \ln (- x)$$

$\frac{\text{d} \ln {\color{Peach} |x|}}{\text{d} x}$
$= \frac{\text{d} \ln (- x)}{\text{d} x}$
$= {\color{Peach} \frac{\text{d} \ln (- x)}{\text{d} (- x)}} \cdot {\color{Peach} \frac{\text{d} (- x)}{\text{d} x}}$
$= {\color{Peach} -} \frac{1}{x} \cdot {\color{Peach} (- 1)}$
$= \frac{1}{x}$

$\blacksquare$
---

## $\alpha _2: a x > 0$

$$\ln |x| = \ln x$$

$\frac{\text{d} \ln {\color{Peach} |x|}}{\text{d} x}$
$= {\color{Peach} \frac{\text{d} \ln x}{\text{d} x}}$
$= \frac{1}{x}$

$\blacksquare$
